  "rationale": "The requirement applies. `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with `name:` front matter, and the `skills` query lists it as a site.\n\nIt meets the obligation. After the front matter and the `# Bootstrap requirements` title, the file has a short unheaded introduction. That introduction is title-level prose, not a section. The first section heading is `## Workflow`, which comes before `## Inventories`, `## Proposing requirements`, `## Tagging`, `## Report` and `## Gotchas`. The Workflow section is a numbered checklist of steps 1 to 9, with sub-steps under step 7. The steps are ordered, and the text before the list says how to repeat them.\n\nThe requirement text has no violation queries, so there were no violation matches to judge.\n\nOne reading is possible: \"open ... with its workflow\" could forbid any prose before the Workflow section. I did not treat that as an equally supported reading. The text says \"before any other section\", and the introduction is not a section. `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` has the same layout: a title, then `section[Workflow]` as its first child section.",
